mapping "SJB.1" source="SJB" target="d451" relationship=equivalent {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
 comment "en" """
 Source SJB is a KSI activity node (parent of the SJB.*
 intervention children). Target ICF d451 has the identical Swedish name
 the local ICF mirror's designation — name-for-name equivalence.
 Both denote the single functional activity of climbing up and down stairs. Exact-equivalent tier
 : the KSI source adopts the ICF term verbatim, a verified 1:1 equivalence.
 """ suspect=quoted-text
}
mapping "SJB.AA.ZZ.1" source="SJB.AA.ZZ" target="d451" relationship=related_to {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
 comment "en" """
 Source SJB.AA.ZZ is a KSI assessment
 (Bedömning) activity targeting stair-climbing — a social-service intervention act, not the
 function itself. ICF has no concept for 'assessment of stair-climbing'; the only related
 standard concept is d451 the imported designation, which denotes the underlying
 function the assessment is about. Related link : the source is about the d451 domain
 (assessment-of), not a case of it; recorded as a reviewer lead per the related-vs-no_match
 boundary rule (the clinical association is real and defensible).
 """ suspect=quoted-text
}
mapping "SJB.AM.ZZ.1" source="SJB.AM.ZZ" target="d451" relationship=related_to {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
 comment "en" """
 Source SJB.AM.ZZ is a KSI observation
 activity for stair-climbing — an intervention/assessment act, not the function. ICF d451 is the underlying functional concept the observation concerns.
 Related link : source is about the d451 domain; no ICF equivalent for the observation act
 itself.
 """ suspect=quoted-text
}
